","urn:nuls:31786100700548"],"lc_classifications":["RC516 .J363 1995","RC516.J363 1995"],"key":"/books/OL19294117M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL443429A"}],"publish_places":["New York"],"subjects":["Jamison, Kay R. -- Mental health.","Depression -- Personal Narratives."],"genres":["Personal Narratives."],"source_records":["marc:marc_openlibraries_phillipsacademy/PANO_FOR_IA_05072019.mrc:40190895:1083","marc:marc_openlibraries_sanfranciscopubliclibrary/sfpl_chq_2018_12_24_run02.mrc:110297374:1476","amazon:0679443746","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part24.utf8:100944400:1002","ia:unquietmind0000jami_o7l5","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2022-03-17","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-009.mrc:53802535:2277","marc:marc_nuls/NULS_PHC_180925.mrc:122941832:1091","idb:9780679443742","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-004.mrc:251402925:2064","bwb:9780679443742","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_037.bib.mrc:337635577:4585"],"title":"An unquiet mind","lccn":["97072663","95014273"],"number_of_pages":223,"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"isbn_10":["0679443746"],"publish_date":"1996","publish_country":"nyu","by_statement":"Kay Redfield Jamison.","works":[{"key":"/works/OL2910908W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"ocaid":"unquietmind0000jami_o7l5","oclc_numbers":["32312965"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"From Kay Redfield Jamison - an international authority on manic-depressive illness, and one of the few women who are full professors of medicine at American universities - a remarkable personal testimony: the revelation of her own struggle since adolescence with manic-depression, and how it has shaped her life.\n\nVividly, directly, with candor, wit, and simplicity, she takes us into the fascinating and dangerous territory of this form of madness - a world in which one pole can be the alluring dark land ruled by what Byron called the \"melancholy star of the imagination,\" and the other a desert of depression and, all too frequently, death.\n\nA moving and exhilarating memoir by a woman whose furious determination to learn the enemy, to use her gifts of intellect to make a difference, led her to become, by the time she was forty, a world authority on manic-depression, and whose work has helped save countless lives."},"latest_revision":16,"revision":16,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-10-21T13:14:03.637271"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-05-11T17:16:34.684332"}},{"publishers":["A.A. Knopf"],"number_of_pages":223,"ia_box_id":["IA117911"],"isbn_10":["0679443746"],"subject_place":["United States"],"covers":[418470],"lc_classifications":["RC516 .J363 1995"],"latest_revision":11,"key":"/books/OL782327M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL443429A"}],"ocaid":"unquietmind00jami","publish_places":["New York"],"lccn":["95014273"],"uri_descriptions":["Contributor biographical information","Sample text","Publisher description"],"edition_name":"1st ed.","pagination":"223 p. ;","source_records":["marc:marc_records_scriblio_net/part25.dat:1741045:1002","marc:marc_ithaca_college/ic_marc.mrc:142089088:754","ia:unquietmind00jami"],"title":"An unquiet mind","url":["http://www.loc.gov/catdir/bios/random057/95014273.html","http://www.loc.gov/catdir/samples/random041/95014273.html","http://www.loc.gov/catdir/description/random041/95014273.html"],"identifiers":{"librarything":["3177"],"goodreads":["320341"]},"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-01T03:28:50.625462"},"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"dewey_decimal_class":["616.89/5/0092","B"],"subjects":["Jamison, Kay R. -- Mental health","Manic-depressive persons -- United States -- Biography","Women college teachers -- United States -- Biography"],"publish_date":"1995","publish_country":"nyu","last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2011-08-12T18:34:59.072188"},"by_statement":"Kay Redfield Jamison.","works":[{"key":"/works/OL2910908W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"uris":["http://www.loc.gov/cat